# Generated by mt5_export_deals.py each Friday — regenerable from the terminal,
# so there is no reason to version a new one every week.
# mt5_trades_2026-08-02.csv IS committed: it is the reference copy showing the
# expected column shape, and the export that exposed the 13-vs-42 gap.
mt5_deals_*.csv

# Python bytecode — machine-local and regenerated on import. Was tracked by
# accident (gate_outcomes.cpython-314.pyc); a committed .pyc can shadow an
# edited .py on another machine and silently run stale gate logic.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
